      "writtenOn": "2018-04-20T21:47:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this is a good idea for POWER_GOOD. What about when we\u0027re warm resetting (either short or long)? Won\u0027t this signal go low temporarly, making he EC think the pmic lost power? I\u0027m thinking it might be better to use PS_HOLD for this, or maybe an OR between both of those. We also have to think how the long warm reset will affect these signals, since we\u0027ll temporarily have to mux them to outputs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "0c99dd3e1d433d117911d96e426c04400b709cd6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "040da758_a0c66d39",
        "filename": "board/cheza/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
