      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-21T01:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a good point. But PS_HOLD still has the same issue, which is a low pulse for warm reset. Looked at an example, it is like:\n 1. PS_HOLD L\n 2. AP_RST_L L\n 3. AP_RST_L H\n 4. PS_HOLD H\n\nMaybe we need to add some timer logic to ignore the short pulse.\n\nStill need to experiment your rev-1 design for the long warm reset case. I think it is probably OK. For the long warm reset, which is controlled by SYS_RST_L as an EC input, the falling edge will trigger S0-\u003eS5 and the raising edge will trigger S5-\u003eS0. The AP_RST_L signal is held by EC during the process, should match what we want.",
      "parentUuid": "59967774_88876b20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "0c99dd3e1d433d117911d96e426c04400b709cd6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
